{
  "requirement": "Marks an agent request that has begun collecting node contents. Further node inputs can be added before awaiting the answer.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct NodePhase;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.NodePhase` has two obligations. (1) `NodePhase` marks an agent request that has begun collecting node contents. (2) More node inputs can be added before the answer is awaited.\n\n**Obligation 1 (marker for a request that has begun collecting node contents).** The marked test is `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]`. It enters the node phase with `ctx.ask::<Answer>().context(..).contents_of_current_node()`. The entry methods are `contents_of_current_node` and `contents_of_successors`, both in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs`. Each returns `Ask<.., NodePhase>`. Other tests enter the phase through `contents_of_successors` as the first insertion:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[string_and_str_contexts_deliver_identical_prefixes_and_fingerprints]`\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]`\n\n**Obligation 2 (further inputs can be added before awaiting).** The marked test chains `.contents_of_successors(7).contents_of_current_node()` onto the `NodePhase` request. It then converts to a future with `into_future()` and awaits it. Its assertions check these outcomes:\n- The agent receives `[(1,subject),(3,implementation),(2,test),(3,implementation),(1,subject)]`. This shows all later inputs were accepted, in order and with repetition.\n- The graph reads are `[1,3,2,3,1]`.\n- The recorded dependencies match.\n- The future is `Send`.\n\nThe `NodePhase` doc-tests, which cite `judge.phases`, add `compile_fail` checks that `.context` cannot be called after entering the node phase. The requirement does not demand these checks, but they support the phase-marker semantics.\n\n**Public export.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks that the `pub struct NodePhase` export exists and matches the specification.\n\nI found no plausible violation of the requirement text that these tests would accept. The type is a plain marker, so no further behavior needs testing.",
  "references": "909f09d5168c839a764d052216fd8a81d52222d7dce5a9a991746bb17ad69803",
